.TH "COMPRESS.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
compress.sh \- create a compressed archive using its filename extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBcompress.sh ARCHIVE FILE...\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Choose tar, zip or rar based on ARCHIVE suffix and archive the remaining FILE arguments. Recognised suffixes: .tar, .tar.bz2, .tar.xz, .tar.gz, .tgz, .zip and .rar. Unrecognised suffixes currently produce no diagnostic.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
compress.sh backup.tar.gz Documents/Projects
compress.sh files.zip file1 file2
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
extract.sh(1)
